From 8ba0719e340fa6e7fb7db6a863d92d00a319eadd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefano Borghini <projects@stefanoborghinidesign.it>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 16:06:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add /become-a-partner B2B landing page and site nav

New operator-facing landing page (Base/Premium/Signature plans,
selection philosophy, FAQ, and a real application form backed by
Supabase + Turnstile + an owner notification email), plus a shared
PublicHeader nav (Home/Configurator/How It Works/For Operators/
Contact) now used on the homepage and this new page.

- src/app/become-a-partner: page + client component
- src/app/api/partner-application: verifies Turnstile, inserts into
  the new partner_applications table, emails the owner
- supabase-migrations/2026_partner_applications.sql: new table,
  RLS locked to server-side service-role inserts only
- src/components/layout/PublicHeader.tsx: shared nav, wired into the
  homepage in place of its old logo-only nav
- New "nav" and "becomePartner" namespaces in src/messages/en.json
  (site_copy/Lara pipeline, same as the rest of the site)
- /start's Work With Us link now points here instead of the mailto
  placeholder

Requires running the new SQL migration and seed-site-copy.mjs before
the page has real copy and can accept submissions.
